Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 58 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   EXTENDING TO THE SURGICAL MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  Note  The tumor mass is 2cm in greatest dimension  Histologically  multiple geographically separate foci of infiltrating tumor are present  The tumor is almost entirely infiltrating  with only a small focus of in situ carcinoma  The infiltrating component has a predominantly alveolar pattern  Lymphatic invasion is present  The alveolar pattern raises the possibility of neuroendocrine differentiation  Positivity of the tumor cells for synaptophysin by immunoperoxidase lends some support to this  However  the tumor is negative for chromogranin  and a Grimelius stain is negative  Diagnosis by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 01                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 243 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Positive 61 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 34     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  EXCISION   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast mass  is a 5 0x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast biopsy specimen  The external surface is inked and sectioned to reveal a red tan  fleshy  well defined lobular mass with a white rim that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  It is focally at the margin  Representative section is submitted as frozen section  1 and the frozen block is saved frozen  Tissue is also taken for estrogen receptor studies as well as BRDU studies  The remainder is submitted in A through G  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS   CARCINOMA  PROBABLY OF DUCTAL ORIGIN  O R  Resident  Jay Austen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 18 20 CLINICAL DATA  Large left breast tumor  atypical pathology    sarcomatous cancer      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  CORRECTED ADDENDUM TRANSCRIPTION ERROR Revised by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Revised on 09 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 09 55                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  SARCOMATOID  SPINDLE CELL  CARCINOMA  MARGINS NEGATIVE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  The tumor is composed predominantly of spindle cells  with rare epithelioid neoplastic elements  Using immuno  peroxidase methods on two sections  the spindle shaped and epithelioid cells both stain for keratin 903  but are negative for several other keratins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2  Keratin 7  wide spectrum keratin   The tumor cells also are positive for vimentin  smooth muscle actin and muscle actin  faint   and negative for desmin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID protein  epithelial membrane antigen  carcinoembryonic antigen and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Together with the ultrastructural features  see addendum   the findings indicate that many of the spindle cells show epithelial differentiation  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   REMOVED_CASE_ID  AND  REMOVED_CASE_ID    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NO CYTOKERATIN POSITIVE TUMOR CELLS ARE IDENTIFIED ON IMMUNOSTAINS OF THREE LEVELS OF EACH OF TWO BLOCKS  K L   LYMPH NODE  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY  SENTINEL  223   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  ONE NODE   THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NO CYTOKERATIN POSITIVE TUMOR CELLS ARE IDENTIFIED ON IMMUNOSTAINS OF THREE LEVELS  M   Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Edited by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 39 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Ben Zion Pilch  M D  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                     ELECTRON MICROSCOPY Addendum          ELECTRON MICROSCOPY ADDENDUM    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  SARCOMATOID  SPINDLE CELL  CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  Note  The tumor is composed of spindle shaped cells  Many of the cells have the features of myofibroblasts with intracytoplasmic filaments and dense bodies  Some cells  however  contain intracytoplasmic tonofibrils confirming their epithelial differentiation  The findings are consistent with a spindle cell carcinoma  Added by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 10 06    REVISED REMOVED_DATE        RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block W   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of adipose tissue  which is dissected to reveal two lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE and 2 3cm in greatest dimension  Each lymph node is bisected and frozen entirely as frozen section  1  and now in cassette K and frozen 