that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in two separately labeled parts  Received in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue with a stitch designating the tumor site  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm ill defined  tan  slightly firm and granular mass that is present at the inked margin  A representative section of the mass is frozen as FX 1  now A  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is soft  yellow white and unremarkable  The remainder of the mass is submitted in B through D  Representative sections of the biopsy is submitted in E and F  Received on the back bench   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a 28 x 15 x 3 0cm right modified mastectomy specimen  The right breast is 19 x 15 x 3 0cm with an overlying skin ellipse which is 18 x 9cm  The skin ellipse contains a 0 8cm unremark