TOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block B   Some tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Some tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   to strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  29 MAY 03 at 13 30     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block B   HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of breast tissue with a short suture designating the superior margin and a long suture designating the lateral margin  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior margin inked black  the superior margin inked green  the inferior margin inked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm poorly defined tan  gritty mass which comes to REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE  approximately REMOVED_DATE  approximately 4 0cm from the anterior  posterior  inferior  superior  medial  lateral margins respectively  The remaining breast parenchyma is tan yellow and fibrofatty with the fibrous areas displaying a cystic  granular surface  Representative sections are submitted as follows to include the entire mass  A  Mass to anterior and posterior margins  B  Mass to anterior and inferior margins  C  Mass to anterior margin to include area of biopsy clip  D  Cystic and granular parenchyma to anterior and posterior margins  E  Cystic and granular area to anterior margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of tan pink adipose tissue within which multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from 0 4cm to 1 3cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  F  1 lymph node bisected  G  1 potential lymph node  H  3 whole lymph nodes  I  3 whole lymph nodes  J  5 whole lymph nodes  K  2 whole lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin lateral half of cavity  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of tan pink fibroadipose tissue which is submitted in its entirety as L P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin medial half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of tan pink fibroadipose tissue which is submitted in its entirety as Q V  Gross Description by  CHRISTOPHER MASON Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLA  DISSECTION PART C  BREAST LEFT SHAVED MARGINS LATERAL REMOVED_DATE CAVITY  EXC PART D  BREAST LEFT SHAVED MARGINS MEDIAL REMOVED_DATE CAVITY  EXCI , Uncheck