Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient  MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE  Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1  Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D   Resident  Michiya Nishino  M D   Frozen Section Pathologist  Judith A Ferry  M D   Frozen Section Resident  Jessica Wang  M D   Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D              Addended Report                Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results  Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH   Results  CLINICAL DATA   Right poorly differentiated  invasive ductal carcinoma  ER PR Her 2 negative   Status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   RESIDUAL INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA  WITH NEOADJUVANT TREATMENT EFFECT     NOTE  The residual cancer is mostly present in a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm mass   gross measurement  that is composed of a central partly organized hematoma  surrounded by a dense shell of sclerotic  edematous  partly necrotic  and  slightly chronically inflamed tissue with dystrophic calcification  The  residual tumor cells are few in number and are scattered in this peripheral  shell of tissue  as isolated single and compact clusters of large epithelioid  cells with bizarre nuclear characteristics  with some mitotic activity   Abutting the mass is a hyalinized fibroepithelial lesion with dystrophic  calcification and also regions of residual carcinoma cells  both invasive and  in situ   probably representing a fibroadenoma partially involved by tumor   The neoplastic cells appears to be grade 2 to 3  but the evaluation of grade  and overall tumor size is hampered by the prior administration of chemotherapy   The tumor cells are within 0 1cm of the posterior margin  Parenchyma away  from the mass appears atrophic  This case also was reviewed at an MGH breast  pathology division conference on REMOVED_DATE     The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone  receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ  hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  will be  reported in an addendum     BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR FLAP   EXCISION   UNREMARKABLE FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY     LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   EXCISION   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO OF TWO NODES  0 2   SEE NOTE   THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED     NOTE  To evaluate for metastatic carcinoma  immunohistochemical stains for  cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin were examined on levels  from each of three blocks  The findings support the above diagnosis     GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received are 3 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN     Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right axillary sentinel  node   are 2 lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm   respectively  The smaller lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1   now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The larger lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1A  now  as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining fibroadipose tissue is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 2cm  mastectomy  specimen with a suture designating the 12 o clock position  A REMOVED_DATE x 10 5cm   ellipse of skin overlies a round  fluctuant mass in the upper outer quadrant   externally measuring 10cm in greatest dimension and spanning from the 7  o clock to 11 o clock position  and extending from the lateral aspect of the  areolus to 11 5cm from the nipple  A 0 4cm  well healed scar overlies the  center of the mass  The nipple is unremarkable  On sectioning  the mass is  9 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm  round  multicystic  hemorrhagic  soft  and in the  upper outer and lower outer quadrants  1 1cm of the anterior margin  5 5cm  from the lateral margin  15 5cm from the medial margin  and  0 1cm from the  posterior margin  It is surrounded by a tan white and focally calcified rim  measuring 0 8cm in greatest thickness  The cystic spaces are filled with  serosanguineous fluid  Abutting this mass  superiorly  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm  soft tan white area located 4 5cm from the posterior margin  with  calcification  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  Lymph  nodes are not detected in the lateral tissue  The following representative  sections are submitted      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cystic mass to posterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cystic mass to anterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cyst wall from center of the specimen    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of calcified rim of cystic mass  after  decalcification     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area of tan white soft parenchymal change  6 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm       Received in formalin  labeled  right breast additional inferior flap   is an  8 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm  piece of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is  not oriented  Representative sections of the specimen  approximately 40  of  the submitted tissue   are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS   FROZEN SECTION  1   1A   RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  2 LYMPH NODES         Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Friday  REMOVED_MONTH 23   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06 03 13PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses       