king the anterior margin and a short stitch marking the superior margin  Specimen is oriented along the superior inferior axis and inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  lateral yellow  Serial sectioning shows the previous biopsy site with a firm  ill defined stellate mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm within a dense area of fibrous tissue  The mass is located 0 5cm from the superior tip and 0 5cm from the inferior tip  it abuts the posterior margin and is 0 3cm from the lateral margin  0 7cm from the medial margin  and  1 0cm from the anterior margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior tip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior tip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor  almost entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of area away from biopsy site  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  final superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty soft tissue fragment with a stitch marking the new margin  This is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  final medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fibrofatty soft tissue fragment with a stitch marking the final margin  This is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  final deep   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty soft tissue fragment with a stitch marking the final margin  This is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  final inferior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fibrofatty soft tissue fragment with a stitch on the new margin  This is inked black  Specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  final lateral   are two fibrofatty soft tissue fragments  unoriented  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain   1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over expression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  156  to chromosome 17 signals  137  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE  2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results   Lymphoma Workup RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STUDIES ON PARAFFIN SECTIONS  Studies performed at MGH  The lymph node architecture is effaced by a proliferation of small lymphocytes  Scattered pale staining areas are seen containing larger cells  prolymphocytes  paraimmunoblasts   consistent with proliferation centers  With B lineage antibodies  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and PAX 5  there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and are negative for cyclin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Residual reactive follicles at the periphery of the lymph node are bcl6   With T lineage antibody  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of many small cells scattered within the tissue  A stain for Ki67 shows an appropriately high level of staining in reactive follicles  The lymphoma cells show a very low proliferation index   5    with slightly increased staining within proliferation centers  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of SMALL LYMPHOCYTIC LYMPHOMA  CONSISTENT WITH CHRONIC LYMPHOCYTIC LEUKEMIA  NOTE  Dr  Aliyah Rahemtullah has reviewed the lymph node specimens and concurs with the diagnosis of chronic lymphocytic leukemia small lymphocytic lymphoma  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  3 by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION PART F  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL DEEP MARGIN   EXCISION PART G  BREAST  report_end  , Checked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 06 CLINICAL DATA  Firm left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  75   SPANNING A REGION REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN IN TINY FOCI  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOLID AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPE  25   OCCUPYING EIGHT OF ELEVEN SECTIONS AND EXTENDING TO MANY MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion are not seen  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the slides and agrees with this interpretation  BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  2   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ADENOSIS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  MICROCYSTS  AND FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  Diagnosis by  Julie Fanburg  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 04 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue with short stitch on superior and long stitch on lateral margin  Lateral margin is inked red  the remainder inked black  The tissue is serially sectioned from superior to inferior  Sectioning reveals a 1 0cm stellate  tan  firm area with a central depression  Representative sections frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The rest of the breast parenchyma is submitted in A through K  with the firm stellate area in C through F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy  2   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose with a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture designating the new inferior margin  The new inferior margin is inked red and the remaining tissue is inked black  submitted entirely in L through O  medially to laterally  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST PART B  BREAST  2  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
