val is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 12 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm unoriented fibrofatty breast tissue with a localization needle in place  and an accompanying radiograph  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to display a predominately tan pink dense fibrous tissue with a minimal amount of tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A D with the area of calcifications in cassette B C  Also received in the same container  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm unoriented fibrofatty breast tissue which is inked serially sectioned and entirely submitted as E  Gross Description by  JAMES BARRY Resident  Grace T  McKee MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 12 38 CLINICAL DATA  Re excision of breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 11 40                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 7cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue partially surfaced anteriorly by a REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan skin ellipse which has a 3 7cm well healed linear scar running through it  There is a short suture designating anterior  a bow tie designating cephalad  and a long suture designating lateral  The anterior aspect is black inked  the posterior is blue inked  The posterior aspect is opened to reveal a red brown focally indurated surface  Contiguous with this area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm hemorrhagic cavity with surrounding fat necrosis  The cavity extends to within 0 6cm of the anterior  0 6cm of the superior  0 1cm of the posterior  0 5cm of inferior  1 0cm of the lateral  and 1 5cm of the medial margins  Residual tumor is not grossly identified  The remaining parenchyma is predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue admixed with thin white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from lateral to medial as follows  SECTION CODES  A  Lateral most margin  B  Cavity to inferior margin  C  Cavity to superior margin  D  Cavity to superior posterior margin  E  Cavity to posterior margin  F  Cavity and granular tissue to posterior margin  H L  Representative sections  Gross Description by