ry  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  with a localizing wire and x ray showing clusters of coarse calcifications at one margin  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an area of white gray  gritty tissue  abutting an inked margin  0 4 x 0 2cm    No frozen section done  Suspicious areas in cassettes A through C  rest in D through I  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Labeled   1  right breast specimen A  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place and x ray demonstrating clusters of large coarse calcifications  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm cluster of white gray gritty material abutting an inked margin  No frozen section done  The specimen is too small to freeze  Lesion submitted in cassettes J  K and the remainder submitted entirely in cassettes L through Q  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast  B  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place  an x ray demonstrating vague radio density at one end of the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a gray pink gritty fairly well circumscribed nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm extending to within 0 2cm of the inked margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  The lesion is submitted in cassettes R through V  the remainder is submitted entirey in cassettes W through GG  No frozen done  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT   NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST A  BIOPSY  NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST B  BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  NO FROZEN SECTION DONE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Simon Bergman  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST PART B  RIGHT BREAST A PART C  RIGHT BREAST B   report_end  , Unchecked.
