ked as follows  superior aspect green  inferior yellow  posterior black  anterior blue  Cut section reveals predominantly in the lateral aspect a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm cavity with white fibrotic to dark red hemorrhagic borders  Surrounding the cavity are multiple foci of fat necrosis  The cavity is 0 4cm from the posterior margin  REMOVED_DATE from the inferior  REMOVED_DATE from the anterior  and REMOVED_DATE from the superior  The remainder of the cut surface is soft  yellow lobulated fat  Entirely submitted from lateral to medial as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three transections sequentially from lateral margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One single transection bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single medial aspect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One transection bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One transection bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One transection bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One transection bisected  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  deep margin   are two portions of fibrofatty breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  One side of both tissues is hemorrhagic with tan soft friable  adherent tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned  and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Holly A Brunner  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Holly A Brunner  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Holly A Brunner  on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note