s laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 96 at 09 26     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   favorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 6 x 4 x 2cm portion of fibrofatty tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  tan yellow circumscribed nodule within firm  white parenchyma  The nodule is within 0 2cm of the margin  A portion of the nodule is frozen as FX  1 and submitted in cassette M  The remainder of the nodule is submitted in cassettes A through E  The parenchyma in its entirely in F through L  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST BIOPSY  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
