rms of axillary involvement  None  NOTE  The metastatic tumor cells are present in association with sclerosis  likely due to prior treatment effect  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm unoriented portion of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a needle localization wire in place  The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan white  ill defined  soft to firm and focally cystic irregular mass which grossly abuts the overlying inked margin  The adjacent breast parenchyma shows foci of fat necrosis  The metallic clip is not grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  mass to overlying inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  breast parenchyma  away from mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Opposite margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of breast parenchyma Received are four containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast cephalad final margin   is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which is serially sectioned and submitted in toto in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast caudad final margin   is an unoriented  irregular portion of yellow  lobulated fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which is serially sectioned and submitted in toto in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast medial final margin   is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which is serially sectioned and submitted in toto in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left breast final lateral margin   is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which is serially sectioned and submitted in toto in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary nodes  contents    is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  which is dissected and palpated to reveal 19 possible lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  All candidate nodes are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each containing one possible node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two possible nodes  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three possible nodes  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each containing four possible nodes  submitted entirely  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL CEPHALAD MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL CAUDAD MARGIN   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION PART F  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  report_end  , Unchecked.
