ogesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  accompanied with a radiograph   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  It is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined  tan to white  slightly gritty area extending to the margin  measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 5cm  Entirely submitted in A through J  with the suspicious area in A through H  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  NO GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS LESION FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA IDENTIFIED  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
