Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 07 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  INVASION  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  TWO NODULES  REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE DEEP MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   EXTENSIVE  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm left breast excision with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm overlying skin ellipse and a 2 0cm incision in the skin  There is a long suture to indicate the lateral margin and a short suture to indicate the superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  Superior margin   blue  medial margin   red  inferior margin   yellow  lateral margin   green  deep margin   black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a small previous biopsy cavity but otherwise unremarkable breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely from superior to inferior in cassettes A through F  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
