ior margin and 0 6cm away from the anterior margin  The fibrous area extends from 2 2cm from the closest anterior margin and abuts the posterior margin  The surrounding tissue is white tan  firm and fibrous  with scattered cysts  the greatest measuring 0 4cm in diameter  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the nodular fibrous area in the upper outer quadrant of the breast  submitted from lateral to medial  with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing 1 cross section   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing another cross section and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing another cross section   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue away from abnormal area  lower inner quadrant  containing potential cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional section away from the abnormal area  lower inner quadrant  containing potential cyst  Received are 3 containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  additional right breast tissue   are multiple fragments of unoriented yellow fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  The cut surface of the specimen is yellow  smooth and unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  right axillary nodes   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm  There are 4 metal clips found in the specimen  11 potential lymph nodes are palpated  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 lymph node candidates  submitted in toto   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node candidate  bivalved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node candidate  bivalved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node candidate  trisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 lymph node candidates  submitted in toto   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of fibroadipose tissue  Received in formalin  labeled  righ