ell as N O  No lymph nodes are found in the axillary portion of the specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Ileal Colon   is an 8 0cm portion of cecum and a 45 0cm portion of attached ileum  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm transmural defect  located at 7 0cm from the ileocecal junction and the surrounding mesentery necrosis and fibrinous adhesions  Opening the specimen reveals that the perforation site has a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm area showing mucosal necrosis with yellow brown discoloration and sharp demarcation from adjacent dark red mucosa  The entire ileal colon specimen is examined to find no definite tumor lesion on the mucosal surface  Sectioning of the mesentery revealed nodular  appearing adhesions and fat necrosis  Also received in the same container is a 10 0cm unoriented portion of small intestine with a side to side anastomosis to a 7 0cm portion of the small intestine  The anastomosis site has a fresh suture  and the mucosa of both small intestine fragments are dark red with edema  SECTION CODE  A   Proximal ileal resection margin  B   Distal colonic resection margin  C   Representative section from the perforation site  D   Representative section from the mesentery  E   Anastomosis site  F G  End from the anastomosis  Gross Description by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  COLON PART B  BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
